    "body": "okay but none of this answers the question.\"queue large core changes and apply their integer points at evenly spaced intervals\" ??????? like yeah, if you do something that regens half your HP obviously your HP jumps to +50. how is that even a problem? most games work that way. the issue is things that should drain or restore bars in tiny continuous amounts -- like stamina regen/drain, just don't. they do it in chunks. why?\n\nSo is the problem the fact that it can only change in increments of ~3.6 degrees or so? Is that even perceptible? Can we overwrite this base game code to treat these like floats so continuous drain/restoration, like with stamina, is actually continuous?",
